    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Energy Usage Data",
    "long_instructions": "You’d like to convert the energy usage data from [the spreadsheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18UwtdBHy_PiAWNgZKEWYslFm9PpX24r9Sw1yivG7gvc/edit?usp=sharing) to a CSV file so that Python programs can more easily work with the data.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Populate `energy.csv` with data from at least three rows from the spreadsheet. Remember to also include a header row with column names!\r\n2. Press “Run” to see a visual representation of the CSV file and verify that it looks like what you expect.",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Create a CSV file for a school's energy usage.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/e71e29a735284b85e65c8239702a5631-eco-house.png",
